    verification suiteMeasuresTheWorkspaceImplementGate : Test { :>> id = "f65effac-511a-4bae-ab7d-4c0df1fdeff4"; :>> title = "Sprint 742 implement gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-18"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "The implement gate is the DoD's own probes plus the ladder: cargo clippy --workspace --release --all-targets clean after format_push_string (render_receipt's rows through write! with std::fmt::Write) and items_after_statements (the import moved to the top of the fn); cargo build --release Finished and target/release/keel-serve.exe refreshed from it; cargo test -p keel-suite --release --lib 64 passed 0 failed; keel suite --help from the copy names --workspace and the [[part]] rows; the detached keel suite . run from the copy printed keel suite: pass - 955 passed, 0 failed; receipt .keel/metrics/suite-receipt.toml (fingerprint 4ea02049b492...) after 1053 seconds, and the receipt reads outcome pass, 23 [[part]] rows, head 019078d3; fp742.py's independent recomputation over the tree equals all 23 digests (23 equal of 23, read while the stub was still running and again after the receipt was written). One test was corrected against its own fixture before it passed: the round-trip test counted [[part]] three times because the receipt header names the table; it now matches the row's opening line. Two hook fires this sprint: the pre-bash hook denied two python heredocs carrying a backslash (D0309/issue372 class); both were rewritten as scratchpad scripts run by path."; }
